---
title: "batch_price_attestation::deserialize_price_info (Pyth Sui Contracts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_skip_product: skip product_identifier (32 bytes, obsolete)
    q_skip_product --> q_fields: deserialize price_identifier, price, conf, expo, ema_price, ema_conf
    q_fields --> q_status: status = price_status::from_u64(deserialize_u8)
    q_status --> q_skip_pub: skip num_publishers, max_num_publishers (obsolete)
    q_skip_pub --> q_times: deserialize attestation_time, publish_time, prev_publish_time, prev_price, prev_conf
    q_times --> q_check_status: status == TRADING
    q_check_status --> q_trading: true, current_price = new(price, conf, expo, publish_time)
    q_check_status --> q_not_trading: false, current_price = new(prev_price, prev_conf, expo, prev_publish_time)
    q_trading --> q_ema_ts: ema_timestamp = publish_time
    q_not_trading --> q_ema_ts_prev: ema_timestamp = prev_publish_time
    q_ema_ts --> q_build: build PriceInfo
    q_ema_ts_prev --> q_build: build PriceInfo
    q_build --> [*]: return PriceInfo

    note right of q_check_status
        INV-001: non-trading status uses prev_price/prev_conf as fallback
        INV-002: EMA timestamp tracks last trading status timestamp
        INV-003: arrival_time = clock_ms/1000 (on-chain timestamp, not attestation)
    end note
